hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18221","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hassan from Mukhayyis ibn Dabyan from a man of Banu Judham from Malik ibn Atahiyah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If you meet a tithe collector kill him."
"18222","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us with this hadith and shortened part of the chain, and he said meaning thereby charity taken without right."
